## 4. Pre-Flight Permissions Check (Readiness Validation)

Before running migrations, the backend performs a pre-flight sanity check:

### 4.1 Target PostgreSQL Permission Check
Verify the target user has permission to create tables, indexes, and insert data:
```sql
-- Check schema create permission (DDL)
SELECT has_schema_privilege(current_user, 'public', 'CREATE') AS can_create_tables;

-- Check lock timeout support
SET lock_timeout = '5s';
```

### 4.2 Source MongoDB Permission Check
Verify source user has read privileges:
```javascript
await db.command({ ping: 1 });
await db.listCollections().toArray();
```
